<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Diagnosis of a visible cervical lesion: punch biopsy at this visit, an HPV test and cytology, a pregnancy test, a blood count and ferritin; a lesion that looks like cancer is biopsied directly rather than managed by the screening algorithm. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Cervical Cancer (Version 1.2027); 2019 ASCCP Risk-Based Management Consensus Guidelines for Abnormal Cervical Cancer Screening Tests and Cancer Precursors (2019) [S]</item><item>Urgent gynecologic oncology consultation, on the day the biopsy result is given: diagnosis, staging, treatment by stage, and fertility and ovarian function counseling. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Cervical Cancer (Version 1.2027); Fertility Preservation in Patients With Cancer: ASCO Clinical Practice Guideline Update (2018) [S]</item><item>Truthful disclosure as she asked: the biopsy result given to her in person, in Spanish, at a visit with time set aside, before anyone else is told; she chooses who is present and who is told; a professional medical interpreter for clinicians who do not speak Spanish, never a family member; information shared step by step, checking what she wants to know. Guideline: Patient-Clinician Communication: American Society of Clinical Oncology Consensus Guideline (2017) [S]</item><item>Iron deficiency anemia: ferrous sulfate daily, a blood count at about one month, a ferritin at the end of the course, and acetaminophen rather than anti-inflammatory painkillers for pelvic pain. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, anemia monograph (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
